Howdy!

With this update (0.1.8) we add a much-requested feature: you can now play with [b]mouse and keyboard[/b], or a [b]PlayStation controller[/b]!

The whole UI now adapts dynamically (and beautifully, I might add!) to what you are using to play. ❤️

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44526788/a3ba06a35f9ec5fba4ed061dc22b1843c967c04a.gif[/img]

Another feedback we received is that it is sometimes hard to remember what your circuits do - for that reason, we introduced a new HUD mod, called “Inputs HUD”. You will find it in the default player inventory on a new game, and for returning players, it is also dropped by the first boss (Smelter Saw Mk-1), so no way to miss it.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44526788/9f5d2f03821870bb0c0619b749bb7f3a3765ef4a.png[/img]

For our beloved returning players, this is a slightly smaller update than the previous one, but we really wanted to have it out before the holidays (🎅), so you can try it out while we focus on what’s coming next…

… fully playable levels, upgrades, and more!!

[h3]How to stay in the loop?[/h3]
[url=https://discord.gg/kNhxCxrgjJ]Discord[/url], of course! 
And as always… Wishlist and Follow on Steam!

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44526788/f602950a1d739f3d507937fe52d82135853ca53a.gif[/img]

Cheers,
Armored Souls Team


[h2]Changelog v0.1.8[/h2]

[h3]Adds: [/h3]
[list]
[*] Added Keyboard and Mouse mapping, logic, icons, and UI;
[*] Added PlayStation controller mapping, logic, icons, and UI;
[*] Added Multishot logic and stats to existing mods (max limit of 100 projectiles per shot);
[*] Added new mods: Inputs HUD, Pause;
[*] Added new dual-stat mods: Strained Offense, Spoiled Bloom;
[*] Added two decimal values to numbers in UI below 100 for better calculations;
[*] Expanded logic to allow mods to have both global (player) and local (circuit) effects.
[/list]
[h3]Changes: [/h3]
[list]
[*] Changed intro message;
[*] Changed disclaimer in Title menu about the controller (from “Required” to “Recommended”);
[*] Changed size of Circuit fonts;
[*] Renamed HUD into “Basic HUD” to accommodate for different HUD mods;
[*] Renamed Health Gain/Drain into “Heath Rate” to improve readability;
[*] Moved player inside boss room, boss wakes on being hit;
[*] Changed Smelter Saw loot to include all new mods;
[*] Changed Player starting inventory to include Inputs HUD and Pause mods.
[/list]
[h3]Balancing:[/h3]
[list]
[*] Removed negative stats on Permadeath Remover.
[/list]
[h3]Fixes:[/h3]
[list]
[*] Fixed bug with speed not affecting speed of projectiles;
[*] Various improvements to text descriptions;
[*] Various graphical fixes.
[/list]

Hello!

With this update ([b]0.1.7[/b]) we introduce larger, [b]multi-slot mods[/b] to the game!

The one you see moving in the gif below is the new Plasma Gun, reforged into [b]Plasma Cannon[/b].

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44526788/a4d210e5a54f81f39d81f1dd5f8792d907a732bc.gif[/img]

These big boys were in the plans from the start, glad to finally have them!

Managing space in the Motherboard will be a bit harder from now, and optimal builds will require more tinkering... or risk-taking 😆

If you are coming back to the demo, a few new mods are waiting for you: you might want to familiarize yourself with the [b]Permadeath Remover[/b] (the big 2x2 mod in the gif) or try out some of the powerful [b]dual-stat mods[/b].

At the same time, it is a rather small update, so please don’t expect too much! Behind the scenes, we are working hard on the first fully playable level and the Forge system, which will be ready later on.

PS: the next small update will be focused on introducing full keyboard controls.

PPS: the Motherboard has changed slightly, so older saves won’t work anymore, sorry!

[h3]How to stay in the loop?[/h3]
[url=https://discord.gg/kNhxCxrgjJ]Discord[/url], of course! 
And as always… Wishlist and Follow on Steam!

